th their locations or lineage. Add coverage for identical lines in unrelated functions.","id":"410f1d2ce1bc35283c3df7d092fb8d7b138dcb4460166da4b4dd4915d64e22c4","intervals":[[992,993]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Match published changes by location, not file-wide line text."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"39b4711272945983ce677369a7e96f50d825cf59","body":"**Emit a JSON result for explicit job execution.**\n\nWhen the selected job completes, this branch returns without calling `write_result`. `process_item` also discards the job result. Consumers receive no JSON artifact for a completed, deferred, or failed repair.\n\nReturn the selected job result and emit it once at the CLI boundary. As per coding guidelines, “Every operation invocation writes machine-readable JSON to stdout.” Based on learnings, defer this P2/Minor correction to a follow-up issue.","id":"23370760bfefd6ec9c83a968eafef9e0e1d49fd6ec125c133f003e1147f18a6d","intervals":[[1279,1280]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Emit a JSON result for explicit job execution."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"7c3d3290579e7bf5434bf3b833fde75130a97b1c","body":"**Keep the interrupt exit code within the I1 contract.**\n\nAt `apps/crq-python/test_deploy_runbook.py:717`, the test requires exit code `130` when `Interrupted.run()` raises `KeyboardInterrupt`. This expectation accepts an unsupported exit code. Expect `1` and align the interrupt handler with that result.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, “Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 thrown error, 2 arg error, 3 needs-human.”","id":"60b93f57875e3a53a81686a62c62d0f93c0a4baa80287e0377944af46abde3af","intervals":[[717,717]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_runbook.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep the interrupt exit code within the I1 contract."}],"head":"4209141965e58a280eecc016216ed7e8561f0